 "tag": "wing-rebuild-mp423-bridge-sweep",
 "_doc": "MP4/23 bridge wing incidence sweep (2D). In s2dw3_mp423 the rebuilt bridge wing is attached at y 0.20 (reversed area / profile area 0.01, Cl 3.95, Cd 0.131) but at y 0.45 its outboard main plane stalls from the leading edge (87-99 % of its suction side reversed, bl and iso) at 4.5-7 deg geometric incidence, under the loaded main stack. Pre-approved remedy: less incidence. The whole outboard bridge (main plane + flap) is turned trailing edge down by 3, 6 and 9 deg about its leading edge (per-case wing_patch), the inboard piece blended from 0 at y 0.20 (attached as is) to the same value at the junction (y 0.29). 2D sections of the front wing at y 0.36, 0.45, 0.55 (bl mesh). The smallest change that keeps the bridge main plane attached goes to the next 3D run (with the rear-wing decision from the 3D mp423_w2).",
